@zhenggen-xu  I have located the root cause of this problem.  

In the log, the host interface is successfully removed
```
NOTICE syncd#SDK: [SAI_HOST_INTERFACE.NOTICE] mlnx_sai_host_interface.c[1075]- mlnx_remove_host_interface: Remove host interface host interface 9
```
However this happens before the lag membership entry is removed.

In the lag removal attempt we see this log line....
```
NOTICE swss#orchagent: :- removeLagMember: Remove member Ethernet16 from LAG PortChannel0003 lid:200000000041c lmid:1b00000000041d
```

Checking the source code for this function [here](https://github.com/Azure/sonic-swss/blob/master/orchagent/portsorch.cpp#L4767)
```
    if (lag.m_bridge_port_id > 0)
    {
        if (!setHostIntfsStripTag(port, SAI_HOSTIF_VLAN_TAG_STRIP))
        {
            SWSS_LOG_ERROR("Failed to set %s for hostif of port %s which is leaving LAG %s",
                    hostif_vlan_tag[SAI_HOSTIF_VLAN_TAG_STRIP], port.m_alias.c_str(), lag.m_alias.c_str());
            return false;
        }
    }
```
`portsorch` correctly identifies that the LAG has an associated VLAN but doesn't realize that the host interface is already gone and attempts to remove the VLAN tag from the host interface anyway. This leads to the error and eventual crash of orchagent as it cannot locate the hostif of the port.

```
ERR swss#orchagent: :- meta_sai_validate_oid: object key SAI_OBJECT_TYPE_HOSTIF:oid:0xd00000000040e doesn't exist
ERR swss#orchagent: :- setHostIntfsStripTag: Failed to set SAI_HOSTIF_VLAN_TAG_STRIP to host interface Ethernet16
ERR swss#orchagent: :- handleSaiSetStatus: Encountered failure in set operation, exiting orchagent, SAI API: SAI_API_HOSTIF, status: SAI_STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER
```
